{"id":"mahabharata-3-168","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":168,"title":"अष्टषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 168 · The demons' illusions","summary":{"en":"The Nivatakavachas send storms of rocks, floods, fire and darkness by magic, and even Matali is shaken. Arjuna dispels each illusion with a divine weapon, though the demons remain hidden.","kn":"ನಿವಾತಕವಚರು ಮಾಯೆಯಿಂದ ಕಲ್ಲುಮಳೆ, ಪ್ರವಾಹ, ಬೆಂಕಿ, ಕತ್ತಲೆಗಳನ್ನು ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಮಾತಲಿಯೂ ಕಳವಳಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನನು ದಿವ್ಯಾಸ್ತ್ರಗಳಿಂದ ಪ್ರತಿ ಮಾಯೆಯನ್ನೂ ನಿವಾರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಆದರೆ ದಾನವರು ಅಡಗಿಯೇ ಇರುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"निवातकवच माया से पत्थरों की वर्षा, बाढ़, आग और अन्धकार भेजते हैं, और मातलि भी विचलित हो जाते हैं। अर्जुन हर माया को दिव्यास्त्र से दूर करते हैं, यद्यपि दानव छिपे रहते हैं।","te":"నివాతకవచులు మాయతో రాళ్లవాన, వరదలు, అగ్ని, చీకటి సృష్టిస్తారు, మాతలి కూడా కలవరపడతాడు. అర్జునుడు ప్రతి మాయను దివ్యాస్త్రంతో తొలగిస్తాడు, అయినా దానవులు దాగే ఉంటారు.","ta":"நிவாதகவசர்கள் மாயையால் கல்மழை, வெள்ளம், தீ, இருள் ஆகியவற்றை அனுப்ப, மாதலியும் கலங்குகிறான். அர்ஜுனன் ஒவ்வொரு மாயையையும் தெய்வீக அஸ்திரத்தால் நீக்குகிறான், ஆனால் அசுரர்கள் மறைந்தே இருக்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"നിവാതകവചന്മാർ മായാവിദ്യയാൽ കല്ലുമഴയും പ്രളയവും തീയും ഇരുട്ടും അയക്കുന്നു; മാതലിപോലും കുലുങ്ങുന്നു. അദൃശ്യരായ രാക്ഷസന്മാർ തുടരുമ്പോഴും, ഓരോ മായയെയും ദിവ്യാസ്ത്രംകൊണ്ട് അർജുനൻ നിഷ്ഫലമാക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.168; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"यक्षयुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Yakshayuddha Parva (Battle with the Yakshas)","verses":[{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततोऽश्मवर्षं सुमहत्प्रादुरासीत्समन्ततः ।\nनगमात्रैर्महाघोरैस्तन्मां दृढमपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a huge rain of stones appeared on every side, with boulders as big as hills, and it pressed me hard."}},{"n":2,"text":"तदहं वज्रसंकाशैः शरैरिन्द्रास्त्रचोदितैः ।\nअचूर्णयं वेगवद्भिः शतधैकैकमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"With swift arrows like thunderbolts, driven by the Indra weapon, I shattered each of those stones into a hundred pieces in the fight."}},{"n":3,"text":"चूर्ण्यमानेऽश्मवर्षे तु पावकः समजायत ।\nतत्राश्मचूर्णमपतत्पावकप्रकरा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the stone-rain was being pulverized, fire arose, and the stone dust fell like showers of sparks."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततोऽश्मवर्षे निहते जलवर्षं महत्तरम् ।\nधाराभिरक्षमात्राभिः प्रादुरासीन्ममान्तिके ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the stone-rain was destroyed, a far greater rain of water came down near me, in streams thick as chariot axles."}},{"n":5,"text":"नभसः प्रच्युता धारास्तिग्मवीर्याः सहस्रशः ।\nआवृण्वन्सर्वतो व्योम दिशश्चोपदिशस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of sharp-forced streams fell from the sky and covered the heavens, the directions and the intermediate directions."}},{"n":6,"text":"धाराणां च निपातेन वायोर्विस्फूर्जितेन च ।\nगर्जितेन च दैत्यानां न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the falling streams, the howling of the wind and the roaring of the daityas, I could make out nothing."}},{"n":7,"text":"धारा दिवि च संबद्धा वसुधायां च सर्वशः ।\nव्यामोहयन्त मां तत्र निपतन्त्योऽनिशं भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The streams, joined to the sky and spread over the earth, kept falling without pause and bewildered me."}},{"n":8,"text":"तत्रोपदिष्टमिन्द्रेण दिव्यमस्त्रं विशोषणम् ।\nदीप्तं प्राहिणवं घोरमशुष्यत्तेन तज्जलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I hurled the blazing, fearsome divine weapon of drying that Indra had taught me, and by it that water dried up."}},{"n":9,"text":"हतेऽश्मवर्षे तु मया जलवर्षे च शोषिते ।\nमुमुचुर्दानवा मायामग्निं वायुं च मानद ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I had destroyed the stone-rain and dried the water-rain, the danavas, O giver of honor, let loose illusions of fire and wind."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततोऽहमग्निं व्यधमं सलिलास्त्रेण सर्वशः ।\nशैलेन च महास्त्रेण वायोर्वेगमधारयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I quenched the fire everywhere with the water weapon, and with the great mountain weapon I held back the force of the wind."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्यां प्रतिहतायां तु दानवा युद्धदुर्मदाः ।\nप्राकुर्वन्विविधा माया यौगपद्येन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that illusion was checked, the danavas, mad for battle, produced many illusions at once, O Bharata."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो वर्षं प्रादुरभूत्सुमहल्लोमहर्षणम् ।\nअस्त्राणां घोररूपाणामग्नेर्वायोस्तथाश्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a hair-raising rain of terrible weapons, of fire, of wind and of stones, appeared."}},{"n":13,"text":"सा तु मायामयी वृष्टिः पीडयामास मां युधि ।\nअथ घोरं तमस्तीव्रं प्रादुरासीत्समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That illusory downpour pressed me in the battle, and then a terrible, dense darkness arose on all sides."}},{"n":14,"text":"तमसा संवृते लोके घोरेण परुषेण च ।\nतुरगा विमुखाश्चासन्प्रास्खलच्चापि मातलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the world was wrapped in that dreadful, harsh darkness, the horses turned aside and Matali faltered."}},{"n":15,"text":"हस्ताद्धिरण्मयश्चास्य प्रतोदः प्रापतद्भुवि ।\nअसकृच्चाह मां भीतः क्वासीति भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"His golden goad fell from his hand to the ground, and fearful, he called out to me again and again, \"Where are you?\" O best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":16,"text":"मां च भीराविशत्तीव्रा तस्मिन्विगतचेतसि ।\nस च मां विगतज्ञानः संत्रस्त इदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sharp fear came over me when he lost his senses, and he, having lost his wits in terror, said this to me."}},{"n":17,"text":"सुराणामसुराणां च संग्रामः सुमहानभूत् ।\nअमृतार्थे पुरा पार्थ स च दृष्टो मयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Long ago, Partha, there was a mighty battle between gods and asuras for the nectar, and I saw it, sinless one."}},{"n":18,"text":"शम्बरस्य वधे चापि संग्रामः सुमहानभूत् ।\nसारथ्यं देवराजस्य तत्रापि कृतवानहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was also a mighty battle at the slaying of Shambara, and there too I served as the charioteer of the king of the gods."}},{"n":19,"text":"तथैव वृत्रस्य वधे संगृहीता हया मया ।\nवैरोचनेर्मया युद्धं दृष्टं चापि सुदारुणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise at the slaying of Vritra I held the horses, and I also saw the dreadful fight with Virochana's son Bali."}},{"n":20,"text":"एते मया महाघोराः संग्रामाः पर्युपासिताः ।\nन चापि विगतज्ञानो भूतपूर्वोऽस्मि पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have attended these terrible wars, Pandava, and never before have I lost my senses."}},{"n":21,"text":"पितामहेन संहारः प्रजानां विहितो ध्रुवम् ।\nन हि युद्धमिदं युक्तमन्यत्र जगतः क्षयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely the Grandsire has ordained the dissolution of creatures, for this fight is fitting for nothing but the world's destruction.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा संस्तभ्यात्मानमात्मना ।\nमोहयिष्यन्दानवानामहं मायामयं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, I steadied myself by my own effort, intending to confound the illusory host of the danavas."}},{"n":23,"text":"अब्रुवं मातलिं भीतं पश्य मे भुजयोर्बलम् ।\nअस्त्राणां च प्रभावं मे धनुषो गाण्डिवस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I said to the frightened Matali, \"See the strength of my arms, and the power of my weapons and of my bow Gandiva."}},{"n":24,"text":"अद्यास्त्रमाययैतेषां मायामेतां सुदारुणाम् ।\nविनिहन्मि तमश्चोग्रं मा भैः सूत स्थिरो भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today by the illusion of my weapons I will destroy this dreadful illusion of theirs and this fierce darkness. Do not fear, charioteer; be steady.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"एवमुक्त्वाहमसृजमस्त्रमायां नराधिप ।\nमोहनीं सर्वशत्रूणां हिताय त्रिदिवौकसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said so, O lord of men, I released an illusion weapon that bewilders all enemies, for the good of the dwellers of heaven."}},{"n":26,"text":"पीड्यमानासु मायासु तासु तास्वसुरेश्वराः ।\nपुनर्बहुविधा मायाः प्राकुर्वन्नमितौजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As those illusions were being crushed, the lords of the asuras, of boundless might, produced many kinds of illusion again."}},{"n":27,"text":"पुनः प्रकाशमभवत्तमसा ग्रस्यते पुनः ।\nव्रजत्यदर्शनं लोकः पुनरप्सु निमज्जति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Light appeared again and was again swallowed by darkness; the world vanished from sight and again sank in water."}},{"n":28,"text":"सुसंगृहीतैर्हरिभिः प्रकाशे सति मातलिः ।\nव्यचरत्स्यन्दनाग्र्येण संग्रामे लोमहर्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"When it was light, Matali, holding the horses well in hand, drove the excellent chariot about in that hair-raising battle."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततः पर्यपतन्नुग्रा निवातकवचा मयि ।\nतानहं विवरं दृष्ट्वा प्राहिण्वं यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the fierce Nivatakavachas leapt upon me, and seeing an opening I sent them to Yama's abode."}},{"n":30,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा युद्धे निवातकवचान्तके ।\nनापश्यं सहसा सर्वान्दानवान्माययावृतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the fight, destroyer of the Nivatakavachas, went on, I suddenly lost sight of all the danavas, who were veiled by their illusion."}}]}]}